# Milestone: M3
# Covers: scopeTag builtin returns the implicit scope tag for the current function
#         call; used with every() to auto-cancel a loop when function exits.
# defer-to: M5 (requires scopeTag builtin, every keyword, and ',' separator runtime)
#
# Reason:
#   'scopeTag' is a builtin that returns the implicit scope tag for the current
#   activation record — not implemented at M3.  The fixture also uses 'every(1s)'
#   reactive looping (M5 reactive runtime) and ',' for concurrent observation
#   (M5 chk driver).
#
# Original urbiscript (activate at M5 with scopeTag + reactive runtime):
# # function f() { var t = scopeTag; t: every(1s) echo("foobar"), sleep(3.5s) }|;
# # f();
# # [00000001] *** foobar
# # ... (see legacy/repos/aldebaran-urbi/tests/2.x/scope-tag.chk)
